# page.pdl - how the {{Title}} board is DRAWN as an editor page (made by game_new_op; the shared engine game_core's `page` verb and the driver read it). A projection: it decides no rule, the ledger never reads it, and it is NOT part of the rules hash.
# The squares, the jumps and the geometry come from board.pdl (TRACK, JUMP, BOARD cols/rows/path); this file only says how they LOOK. Reference with every row explained: @.apps/chutes/rulesets/default/page.pdl.
# HEADER | key | value (the 384x72 RPG Maker atlas: tile_px 24, atlas_cols 16, atlas_tiles 43, rock_slot 36)   PAGE | block | n (cells per square, the page is cols x n by rows x n, at most 64 x 64)   PAGE | start | strip|none
# TILEMAP | floor_a floor_b start ladder_from ladder_to chute_from chute_to | atlas index   LABELS | on|off   LABELCOLOR | text|outline | rrggbb   LABEL | <square> | text   JUMPTEXT | ladder_from|ladder_to|chute_from|chute_to | text with {n} {to} {from}
# Atlas index = row x 16 + col, picked by looking at it (stand-ins, not art): 1 grass, 7 dirt, 8 sand, 35 orange, 38 blue tile, 39 parquet, 40 orange diamond, 41 white stone.
HEADER     | tile_px     | 24
HEADER     | atlas_cols  | 16
HEADER     | atlas_tiles | 43
HEADER     | rock_slot   | 36
PAGE       | block       | 3
PAGE       | start       | strip
TILEMAP    | floor_a     | 1
TILEMAP    | floor_b     | 8
TILEMAP    | start       | 32
TILEMAP    | ladder_from | 38
TILEMAP    | ladder_to   | 39
TILEMAP    | chute_from  | 35
TILEMAP    | chute_to    | 40
LABELS     | on
LABELCOLOR | text        | ffffff
LABELCOLOR | outline     | 000000
JUMPTEXT   | ladder_from | {n}\n^{to}
JUMPTEXT   | ladder_to   | {n}\n<{from}
JUMPTEXT   | chute_from  | {n}\nv{to}
JUMPTEXT   | chute_to    | {n}\n<{from}
LABEL      | 0           | START
